    description: "Surfaced by the emission-parity:F1 / G2 gate (packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_emission_parity_matrix.py). On the uniform injected fixture every mainstream analyzer emits >=1 imports edge except Java (edge_types==[calls]). Locked as a strict-xfail cell (java, edge_imports) in the G2 matrix; the ratchet XPASS-trips when the Java analyzer starts emitting import edges, pointing the maintainer here. Sibling of INV-golap/INV-loguk under the INV-jahiv analyzer-parity META."  # 8b4e
    fields:  # 8b4e
      statement: "The Java analyzer must emit an imports edge for each import declaration, at parity with every other mainstream analyzer; it currently emits zero. Verified on both a stdlib (import java.util.List) and a non-stdlib (import com.example.helper.Formatter) import — only calls edges are produced. C# emits 2 imports edges for using System, proving stdlib imports are edge-worthy in a sibling analyzer."  # 8b4e
      root_cause: "The Java analyzer extracts call edges but never emits an imports edge for import declarations (java.py import handling produces no Edge of type=imports). Every other mainstream analyzer (python/javascript/typescript/go/rust/csharp/swift) emits >=1 imports edge on the same uniform fixture."  # 8b4e
